00:07:18,620 --> 00:07:24,620
Unbreakable is a thriller, drama, mystery film directed by M. Night Shyamalan.

3
00:10:57,931 --> 00:11:03,931
An ordinary man makes an extraordinary discovery when a train accident
leaves his fellow passengers dead — and him unscathed.

4
00:14:37,241 --> 00:14:43,241
The answer to this mystery could lie with the mysterious Elijah Price, a man who
suffers from a disease that renders his bones as fragile as glass.

5
00:18:16,551 --> 00:18:22,551
David Dunn, played by Bruce Willis.

6
00:21:55,862 --> 00:22:01,862
Elijah Price, played by Samuel L. Jackson.

7
00:25:35,172 --> 00:25:41,172
Audrey Dunn, played by Robin Wright.

8
00:29:14,482 --> 00:29:20,482
Joseph Dunn, played by Spencer Treat Clark.

9
00:32:53,793 --> 00:32:59,793
Elijah's Mother, played by Charlayne Woodard.

10
00:36:33,103 --> 00:36:39,103
Dr. Mathison, played by Eamonn Walker.

11
00:40:12,413 --> 00:40:18,413
Unbreakable is a 2000 American superhero thriller film
written, produced, and directed by M.

12
00:43:51,724 --> 00:43:57,724
Night Shyamalan, and starring Bruce Willis, Samuel L.

13
00:47:31,034 --> 00:47:37,034
Jackson, and Robin Wright.

14
00:51:10,344 --> 00:51:16,344
In Unbreakable, David Dunn (Willis) survives a train crash with no injuries,
leading to the realization that he harbors superhuman abilities.

15
00:54:49,655 --> 00:54:55,655
As he begins to grapple with this discovery, he comes to the attention of disabled comic book
store owner Elijah Price (Jackson), who manipulates David to understand him.

16
00:58:28,965 --> 00:58:34,965
Shyamalan organized the narrative of Unbreakable to parallel a
comic book's traditional three-part story structure.

17
01:02:08,275 --> 01:02:14,275
After settling on the origin story, Shyamalan wrote the screenplay as a speculative screenplay with
Willis already set to star in the film and Jackson in mind to portray Elijah Price.

18
01:05:47,586 --> 01:05:53,586
Filming began in April 2000 and was completed in July.

19
01:09:26,896 --> 01:09:32,896
Unbreakable was released on November 22, 2000.

20
01:13:06,206 --> 01:13:12,206
It received generally positive reviews, with praise for Shyamalan's direction, screenplay, its aesthetics, the
performances, the emotional weight of the story, cinematography, and the score by James Newton Howard.

21
01:16:45,517 --> 01:16:51,517
The film has subsequently gained a strong cult following.

22
01:20:24,827 --> 01:20:30,827
A realistic vision of the superhero genre, it is regarded by many as one of
Shyamalan's best films and one of the best superhero films.

23
01:24:04,137 --> 01:24:10,137
In 2011, Time listed it as one of the top ten superhero
films of all time, ranking it number four.

24
01:27:43,448 --> 01:27:49,448
Quentin Tarantino also included it on his list of the
top 20 films released from 1992 to 2009.

25
01:31:22,758 --> 01:31:28,758
After years of development on a follow-up film, a thematic sequel, Split, with Willis
reprising his role as David Dunn in a cameo role, was released in January 2017.

26
01:35:02,068 --> 01:35:08,068
After the financial and critical success of Split, Shyamalan immediately began working on a third film, titled Glass, which
was released January 18, 2019, thus making Unbreakable the first installment in the Unbreakable film series.

27
01:38:41,379 --> 01:38:47,379
The film explores themes of philadelphia, pennsylvania, parent child
relationship, marriage crisis, superhero, train accident.

28
01:42:20,689 --> 01:42:26,689
The tone is mind_bending and emotional and intense.
